---
source: misc/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"uuidgen\")"
---
Create a new UUID value

Usage: uuidgen [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -r, --random                 Generate a random-based UUID (v4)
  -t, --time                   Generate a time-based UUID (v1)
  -6, --time-v6                Generate a time-based UUID (v6), lexicographically sortable
  -7, --time-v7                Generate a time-based UUID (v7), lexicographically sortable
  -m, --md5                    Use MD5 as the hash algorithm (v3)
  -s, --sha1                   Use SHA1 as the hash algorithm (v5)
  -n, --namespace <NAMESPACE>  Namespace UUID or alias (@dns, @url, @oid, @x500)
  -N, --name <NAME>            Name to hash
  -C, --count <COUNT>          Number of UUIDs to generate [default: 1]
  -x, --hex                    Interpret name as a hexadecimal string
  -h, --help                   Print help
  -V, --version                Print version
